<title>INDIA: Indian rupee inactive as banks closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian rupee inactive as banks closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian rupee was inactive in the forex market on Monday as banks in most cities including Bombay, the country's commercial capital, were closed for a local religious holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said only banks in the southern city of Madras were open.</p>
<p>On Friday, the rupee closed at 35.72/73 after being range-bound at 35.685/695 for most of the day, dealers said.</p>
<p>All banks reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay money desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
